From: oveRTOS <noreply@overtos>
Subject: [PATCH] eth_stm32: kick the Linux-personality socket coordinator on RX

The Linux personality's socket coordinator services parked recv/connect/accept
by probing the zsock non-blocking then parking, retrying on its <=5ms event
tick. Wake it the instant a batch of RX frames is handed to the net stack, so a
parked op resumes on frame arrival instead of on the tick (delta F; mirrors the
FreeRTOS eth_rx_task lxp_sock_kick). The symbol is weak, so a non-personality
build (no run loop) links a NULL and skips the call. Race-free because the net
RX threads are cooperative (above the preemptible coordinator).
---
--- a/drivers/ethernet/eth_stm32_hal_common.c
+++ b/drivers/ethernet/eth_stm32_hal_common.c
@@ -56,6 +56,15 @@
 
 const struct device *eth_stm32_phy_dev = DEVICE_DT_GET(DT_INST_PHANDLE(0, phy_handle));
 
+/*
+ * oveRTOS: wake the Linux personality's socket coordinator the instant a batch of
+ * RX frames has been handed to the net stack, so a parked recv/connect/accept resumes
+ * now instead of on its <=5 ms retry tick (delta F, mirrors the FreeRTOS eth_rx_task
+ * kick). Weak: a non-personality build (no run loop) links a NULL and skips the call.
+ * Defined strong by modules/lxp/src/lxp_run.c (lxp_sock_kick) when LXP_ENABLE_NET is set.
+ */
+__attribute__((weak)) void lxp_sock_kick(void);
+
 static void rx_thread(void *arg1, void *unused1, void *unused2)
 {
 	const struct device *dev = (const struct device *)arg1;
@@ -70,6 +79,7 @@
 	while (1) {
 		res = k_sem_take(&dev_data->rx_int_sem, K_FOREVER);
 		if (res == 0) {
+			int delivered = 0;
 			/* semaphore taken and receive packets */
 			while ((pkt = eth_stm32_rx(dev)) != NULL) {
 				iface = net_pkt_iface(pkt);
@@ -80,8 +90,21 @@
 					LOG_ERR("Failed to enqueue frame "
 						"into RX queue: %d", res);
 					net_pkt_unref(pkt);
+				} else {
+					delivered++;
 				}
 			}
+			/*
+			 * oveRTOS: frames delivered to the net stack — wake the Linux
+			 * personality's socket coordinator so a parked socket op resumes
+			 * at once. Race-free: the net RX threads are cooperative (higher
+			 * priority than the preemptible coordinator), so they finish
+			 * delivering to the socket before the coordinator runs and
+			 * re-probes. No frames => no kick (link-quiet coordinator idles).
+			 */
+			if (delivered && lxp_sock_kick) {
+				lxp_sock_kick();
+			}
 		}
 	}
 }
